course: dictionary
lesson: 5736
title: Lotion: a word for skin care
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A lotion is a thick liquid or cream that you rub on your skin. It can protect your skin, soften it or treat it. «Use the cooling lotion an adult gives you» tells you that a grown-up gives you lotion to help your skin feel better.
explain: The words around lotion give clues about what it does. Sun lotion, hand lotion and calamine lotion each tell you what the lotion is for: the sun, dry hands or itchy spots. Ask yourself: what does this lotion do for my skin?
explain: Lotion is a noun. You can say «a lotion» or «lotions», but you can also say «some lotion» when you mean an amount, as in «Put some lotion on your hands.»
fact: Lotion means a thick liquid or cream that you rub on your skin.
fact: «Sun lotion» protects your skin from sunburn, so put it on before you go out.
fact: «Calamine lotion» soothes itchy bites and rashes, and «hand lotion» helps dry skin.
fact: Lotion is a noun, and it can be countable («a lotion») or uncountable («some lotion»).
fact: Keep lotion out of the reach of babies, because they may try to eat creams and wipes.
exercise: «Scratching chickenpox spots can cause scars, so use the cooling lotion an adult gives you.» What is lotion? | A loud noise you hear at night | A type of shoe | *A thick liquid or cream you rub on your skin | A sweet fizzy drink
exercise: Which lotion soothes itchy bites and rashes? | *Calamine lotion | Sun lotion | Shampoo | Hand lotion
exercise: Which lotion protects your skin from sunburn? | Toothpaste | *Sun lotion | Calamine lotion | Hand lotion
test: «Babies try to eat creams and wipes, so lotion is kept out of their reach.» Why is lotion kept out of babies' reach? | *Babies might try to eat it | Babies like to sleep with it | It is a toy for older children | It is too cold for babies
test: Dad says «Put some lotion on your hands.» How much lotion does «some» mean? | Lotion mixed with bath water | Enough to fill the sink | *A small amount of lotion | A whole bottle must be used up
exam: Which sentence about lotion is correct? | Lotion is a loud noise you hear at night | Lotion is a type of bread | Lotion is a sport played outdoors | *Lotion is a thick liquid or cream you rub on your skin
